<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n20386" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Hĕlōrus</span></b>  (or <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Elōrus</span></b> ), i,
			m., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ἔλωρος</span> or <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Hĕlōrum</span></b> ,
			i, n., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ἔλωρον</span>, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a river on the eastern coast of Sicily</i>, now <i>Atellaro</i>, al. <i>Abisso</i>,
				<i><span class="en">Verg.
				A. 3, 698</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Cic. Verr. 2, 5, 34, § 90</span></i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">clamosus,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Sil.
					14, 269</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">flumen Elorum,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plin.
					3, 8, 14, § 89</span></i>
			.—<i>At its mouth</i> was situated the
			city <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Hĕlōrus</span></b>  (<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">El-</span></b> ), i, f., <i><span class="en">Liv. 24, 35
					<i>init.</i></span></i>; <i><span class="en">Plin. 32, 2,
				7, § 16</span></i>; <i>the vale</i> of which
			was called <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Hĕlōrĭa Tempē</span></b> ,
				<i><span class="en">Ov. F.
				4, 477</span></i>; and <i>the inhabitants</i>, <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Hĕlōrīni</span></b>  (<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">El-</span></b> ), <i><span class="en">Cic. Verr. 2, 3, 43, §
		103</span></i>.</div>
